{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Caravans.</b> As its Targum renders — שְׁיָרַת; named for those who travel a road." "<b>And their camels were bearing, etc.</b> Why did Scripture publicize their load? To make known the reward of the righteous — for it is not the way of Arabs to carry anything but naphtha and pitch, whose smell is foul; and for this one they happened to have spices, so that the righteous one should not be harmed by the foul smell." "<b>Balm.</b> Every large collection of spices is called נְכֹאת, and likewise ״וַיַּרְאֵם אֶת כָּל בֵּית נְכֹתֹה״ (II Kings 20) — the storehouse of his spices. And Onkelos translated it as the term שַׁעֲוָה." "<b>Resin.</b> The sap that drips from balsam trees — and it is the נָטָף counted among the ingredients of the incense." "<b>And ladanum.</b> Its name is לוֹטִיתָא in the language of the Mishnah. And our Sages explained it as the root of a herb, and its name is אשטרולוזיאה, in tractate Niddah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:31.550127249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}